7.2.m:
having finger-sprouts originating from the tips of the branches of the red aśoka, / adorned with garments consisting of heaps of its blossoms, / with feet tipped with red water lilies, having rows of nails like jātī flowers, / with charming thighs like plantain trunks, moon-faced and auspicious,
touching the gods with love, like a beloved wife, / with gusts of wind mingled with lotus filaments, enchanting Autumn arrived. / Cast off was her bodice-veil of white clouds; her face was the full moon's orb;
her eyes were blue water lilies, her charming breasts blossomed forth like buds; / her breezes were fragrant with the pollen of various flowers, delighting the minds;
Autumn arrived there for the wedding of the Goddess, / with the tinkling sound of the anklets of calling geese. / Inundating the mountain rocks with extremely cold waters, / the two seasons, Hemanta and Śiśira, arrived with radiant splendor.
When those two seasons had arrived, Himavān, that best of mountains, / showering powdered snow, quickly shone as if made of silver.
